// slot 6: state (uint8)
// slot 7: commits (mapping)
// slot 8: hasRevealed (mapping)
// slot 9: eligibleJurors (mapping)
// slot 10: selectedJurors (address[])
// slot 11: revealCount (uint256)
// slot 12: yesVotes (uint256)
// slot 13: noVotes (uint256)
// slot 14: resolved (bool)
// slot 15: finalVerdict (bool)
// slot 16: stakes (mapping)
// slot 17: commitStake (uint256)
// slot 18: jurorStakes (mapping)

// cases[0] selectedJurors is at slot computed from:
// keccak256(keccak256(caseId . selectedJurors_slot . cases_slot)) + offset_in_array
// Actually for a mapping at slot 10 in the struct, the slot is:
// For cases[0], the struct starts at slot keccak256(key . slot) where slot=1 (mapping slot)
// Actually simpler: the array selectedJurors for case 0 is at keccak256(keccak256(0 . 1) . 10)

